{
	"FileVersion": 3,
	"Version": 23,
	"VersionName": "1.12.2",
	"FriendlyName": "Create a Character System",
	"Description": "KH3-style compatible skeletons for FINAL FANTASY VII REBIRTH mods. A data object lists which skeletons play which skeletons' animations: Animations (KH3 mode), Mesh rebind, or Family (any number of skeletons share their animations both ways), with More Receiving Skeletons, Requires Paks, Adopt Paths and Carry Sockets; and, per character, which animations it plays: battle and field sets built from other characters' sets (with Auto Match of their attacks), moves and limit breaks (one animation or several played one after another), the ATB abilities and limit breaks of each animation pack the character switches to in battle (Create a Character System 3.3), socket stand-ins, kept proportions, field actions (written into the CharaSpec) and cutscenes. Build Moves makes a character's attacks from animations of the project (an imported or retargeted one per attack name, or a clip of one played faster or slower) with the gameplay notifies of the character's own animation of that name (damage, combo and cancel windows), lined up on the hit, plus a muzzle flash and gunshot for shots, and labels them for a chunk (46 by default). The Move Maker (Window > Rebirth Move Maker) makes one attack, ability or limit break at a time from any animation (another character's, the game's or an imported one, put on the character's skeleton keeping his build, keeping his own pose with the animation's motion added over an animation of his own such as his idle, or as that animation of his own leaning into the animation's root motion and moving as it does, for a monster on a person's walks and runs), with its hits set on the animation editor's playhead and each hit's own damage, effect and sound. Apply Socket Stand-ins puts the stand-ins on the project's meshes and Make Chain Assets makes AnimComposites of chained moves. Character Swaps put another character in some CharaSpec rows' place (Cloud in Sephiroth's): Apply To CharaSpec makes their packs spawn him with the voice you pick and their rows describe him (model, voice, effects, sounds, AI, his shared spec, the hand his weapon goes in), and Export Json makes the two skeletons a family (every character keeping its own height with Keep Proportions) and gives the rows the moveset you pick (the replaced character's or his own). Weapon Swaps put another weapon in a character's hands: Apply To CharaSpec makes the replaced weapons' CharaSpec rows describe the weapon their packs spawn (model, shared spec, effects and sounds), so cutscenes with them start, Export Json adds a weapon family so the new weapon plays the old one's cutscene animations, and socket stand-ins let the old weapon's moves hit with the new one. Forms (Create a Character System 3.6) give a character up to 13 forms it changes into in battle with a forms menu in the game's own menu art (hold Triangle, pick one, let go): each plays an animation pack with its own moves and abilities, and can show or hide parts of the model, wear another model with its AnimBlueprint and parts (Build Moves builds that form's moves on its skeleton, a model made facing another way or floating high turned and brought down with its Model Turn and Model Lift), hide the weapons, play effects and sounds as it switches, keep an aura and fly, and have super armor, a time limit shown on screen and a cooldown. Import Key Animations makes Anim Sequences on a skeleton from key animation files (.cacanim) the Create a Character System tools write for animations from other games. Validate checks bones, curves, sockets, the game's bone-hierarchy test and the characters' CharaSpec rows, and shows how the game combines every compat file (Create a Character System 3.3 rules, with a preview of the auto matches); Export Json writes the Create a Character System UE4SS mod's JSON (Mesh rebind pairs can also go into the receiving skeleton's Asset User Data).",
